# =============================================================================
# experiment/tgrad/tgrad_T-20_h1.00_90d_G0.3.opts — 90 days at -20 C, saturated, with a WEAK
# horizontal gradient |dT/dx| = 0.3 K/m (left warm -> right cold).
#
# Sized to COMPETE WITH PORE GEOMETRY RATHER THAN SWAMP IT. Over the two-throat
# geometry's 3.5e-4 m throat separation this gives dT = 1.05e-4 K and
# drho/rho = 1.00e-5, which is 1.1x the geometric drive |d0*dkappa| = 8.76e-6
# between the two throats. So neither driver is a foregone conclusion and which
# one wins is an actual measurement.
#
# The originally requested -3 K/m would have been 11.5x the geometric drive --
# useful for asking "can a gradient override pore geometry", but it answers that
# by overwhelming it rather than by competing. Run this first; -3 K/m is the
# follow-up if the crossover needs bracketing.
#
# PAIR WITH geometry/2D_two_throat_narrow_{left,right}.opts:
#   narrow-LEFT  -> geometry drives narrow(left)->wide(right) = left->right,
#                   the same way as the gradient: REINFORCING.
#   narrow-RIGHT -> geometry drives narrow(right)->wide(left) = right->left,
#                   against the gradient: COMPETING.
# The isothermal pair (tgrad_T-20_h1.00_90d_G0) is the geometry-only reference, and
# the two isothermal runs should be mirror images -- a symmetry check that the
# effect is geometric and not a numerical bias.
#
# Vapour stays NEUMANN (no -flag_BC_rhovfix). Each plug seals its throat, so the
# domain is three pockets, but the MIDDLE one already connects the two plugs'
# facing menisci. That is the transport path, it needs no reservoir, and keeping
# the system closed makes total ice conservation a working correctness gate.
# =============================================================================

-t_final 7.776e6                        # 90 days

-temp -20.0
-humidity 1.00
-grad_temp0 -0.3,0.0,0.0                 # left warm -> right cold, |dT/dx| = 0.3 K/m

-flag_BC_Tfix 1                          # pin left/right walls; top/bottom insulating

-beta_sub0 5.9216e5                      # K&P beta0 at -20 C, alpha_c = 1.341e-2
-d0_sub0 1.0166e-9                        # physical capillary length at -20 C

-dtmax 5.7e2                             # 1.093 * tau_sub (tau_sub = 5.233e2 s)
-dtCFL 1
-dtCFL_dphimax 0.2
